+AETHER AR -- how to play
+========================
+
+Budokai Tenkaichi 3 in your own room, on Meta Quest over Link or Air Link.
+For the illustrated controller guide, click Help in the AETHER AR window on the PC.
+
+FIRST TIME: in the PC window press Help. It opens on "Quest setup - Start here".
+Follow that numbered checklist once; the Controller guide is the second tab.
+
+1. ON THE QUEST: Settings > Physical space > Space setup. Scan your own room,
+   including the walls, floor and desk/table. No room file needs to be downloaded.
+2. ON THE PC: open the Meta Horizon Link app, not the AETHER AR window.
+   In Settings > General, set Meta Horizon Link as the active OpenXR runtime
+   and enable Unknown sources (AETHER AR is not a Meta store app).
+3. ON THE PC: Settings > Beta (or Developer, depending on the app version):
+   Developer Runtime Features = ON: enables the mixed-reality features below.
+   Passthrough over Meta Horizon Link = ON: shows your real room in the headset.
+   Spatial Data over Meta Horizon Link = ON: lets the game read your Quest's
+   walls, floor and furniture. This does not make your room scan public.
+4. ON THE QUEST: Quick Settings > Link > Air Link; pair/connect to your PC.
+   ON THE PC: choose Mode: Room in AETHER AR, then press Start.
+
+The PC's Developer Runtime Features switch is NOT Quest developer mode.
+Quest developer mode/USB debugging are optional, not required for normal play.
+For Quest camera recordings, start recording BEFORE opening Air Link.
+
+Start AETHER AR with the shortcut "AETHER AR" on your desktop, or type AETHER in the
+Start menu. No shortcut? Double-click "AETHER AR.cmd" in the AETHER AR folder
+(C:\AETHER-AR unless you chose another folder).
+
+
+EVERY TIME
+----------
+
+1. In the AETHER AR window on the PC, press Start.
+2. Put the headset on and turn on Link in it: Quick Settings > Link.
+   Wireless: Quick Settings > Link > Air Link -- nothing to set up on the PC for that.
+   The game appears by itself. It waits up to 5 minutes for the headset.
+   Headset already on? Press Start from Link's desktop view.
+3. The first start shows the memory card check and some logos for about 25 seconds.
+4. The fight starts on your desk or table by itself -- look around the room for it.
+   To move it: point a controller at a spot (cyan ring = OK, red = not here) and pull
+   the trigger. In a fight, press both sticks in first.
+5. To end: take the headset off and press Stop in the AETHER AR window.
+
+Keep your disc image (.iso) where it is: AETHER AR reads it every time you play.
+If you moved it, press "Change disc..." in the AETHER AR window and pick it again.
+
+Mode (in the AETHER AR window):
+  Room    the fighters in your room (uses your Quest's Space Setup room)
+  Screen  the whole game on a big floating screen, e.g. for the story mode
+Options > Quick start: straight to the versus menu. Off: start at the title screen for
+the story mode and the rest of the game. (Your progress is saved either way.)
+A setting changed while the game runs counts at the next start: press Restart.
+
+
+QUEST RECORDINGS
+----------------
+
+Use Air Link for the Quest's built-in camera recording. Start the recording in
+Quest Home, then connect through Air Link and start AETHER AR. This was confirmed
+working on the test Quest 3; your PC and Wi-Fi can affect performance.
+
+Known issue: recording over USB Link can cause severe lag or freezing, even in
+the Link menu without AETHER AR running. Dark trails behind fighters have also
+been reported. USB recording is not fixed or validated in this release.
+
+The camera menu and recording shortcut may not work inside Link. Leave Link to
+stop recording in Quest Home. Do not use the power button as a recording fix.
+On the PC: Help > Controller guide > Quest recordings opens this guidance.
+
+
+CONTROLS
+--------
+
+  Quest controller                   PS2 input       What it does
+  ---------------------------------  --------------  ----------------------------------------------
+  Left stick                         Left analog     Move relative to where you look; D-pad in menus
+  Right stick                        Right analog    Passed through to BT3
+  A (right controller)               Cross           Confirm in menus; Cross action in a fight
+  B (right controller)               Circle          Back/cancel in menus; Circle action in a fight
+  X (left controller)                Square          Square action in a fight
+  Y (left controller)                Triangle        Triangle action in a fight
+  Left / right trigger               L1 / R1         Normal BT3 inputs; pull either to place the fight
+                                                    while the placement ray is visible
+  Left / right grip                  L2 / R2         Normal BT3 inputs
+  Left / right stick click           L3 / R3         Normal BT3 inputs; click both to choose the spot again
+  Menu button (left controller)      START           Pause; hold 3 s without grips to update Space Setup
+  Both grips + Menu                  L2 + R2 + START Switch between Room and Screen mode
+  Select                             Not mapped     Quest controllers have no separate Select button
+
+In combat, the game assigns Cross / Circle / Square / Triangle actions by character and situation.
+Triggers do not confirm menu choices; use A (Cross).
+
+
+IF SOMETHING DOES NOT WORK
+--------------------------
+
+The line under the Start button always says what is happening. When the game cannot go
+on, a box on the PC screen says what to change -- take the headset off and read it.
+
+- The window says the Meta Horizon Link app needs something:
+  the PC app is "Meta Horizon Link" (formerly Meta Quest Link). Open it on the PC:
+    Settings > General > OpenXR Runtime > Set Meta Horizon Link as active
+    Settings > Beta > turn on "Developer runtime features",
+                     "Passthrough over Meta Horizon Link" and
+                     "Spatial data over Meta Horizon Link"
+  Then press Start again.
+
+- "Waiting for the headset" and nothing happens:
+  put the headset on and turn on Link in it (Quick Settings > Link).
+  Still waiting with the headset on? Turn on the light -- the headset cannot track in
+  the dark.
+
+- "No room came from the headset":
+  in the headset open Settings > Physical space > Space setup and set up this room
+  (walls, desk or table, couch). Then press Start. Or choose Mode: Screen to play
+  without the room.
+
+- The fight is in a strange place:
+  look around the room for a few seconds, then press both sticks in, point at your
+  desk or the floor and pull the trigger.
+
+- A black, slightly offset shadow behind the fighters or the aiming ray:
+  that is how Link sends the picture unless its edge fix is on. AETHER AR turns it on
+  for you (a Link setting for your Windows user). The line "Link passthrough edge fix"
+  in the AETHER AR window says where it stands; if it says Link restarts at the next
+  Start, press Start (Link restarts once; turn Link on in the headset again).
+  To turn it off: Options > "Link passthrough edge fix".
+
+- The headset shows a black or frozen picture while the game runs on the PC:
+  that is Link, not AETHER AR. Press Stop, turn Link off and on in the headset (or
+  restart the headset and the Link app on the PC), then press Start.
+
+- "Your ISO is not at ... any more" / "Game disc ... is missing":
+  plug in the drive it was on, or press "Change disc..." and pick it again.
+
+- The game stopped unexpectedly: press Start again. If it happens again, press
+  "Report a problem" in the AETHER AR window. It saves AETHER-AR-report-<date>.zip on
+  your desktop (AETHER AR's logs and settings, your graphics card) -- email that file to
+  contact@aether-xr.com, with a sentence about what happened.
+
+- Something else is broken: press "Repair..." in the AETHER AR window. It builds
+  AETHER AR again from your disc and takes 30-60 minutes.
+
+- The headset battery runs low: a PC's USB port charges the headset only slowly, so a
+  long session on the cable still drains it.
+
+
+OPTIONAL: DEVELOPER MODE
+------------------------
+
+You do not need this to play. It only adds two extras in the AETHER AR window:
+  - "Turn the Quest boundary off while playing" (under Options), and
+  - the headset details line (worn or asleep, Link running, battery).
+
+To use them:
+1. Turn on developer mode for the headset: in the Meta Horizon app on your phone,
+   Devices > your headset > Headset settings > Developer mode. (It needs a free Meta
+   developer account.)
+2. Connect the headset to the PC with the USB cable, put it on and allow USB debugging
+   ("Always allow").
+3. Without the cable: press Options > "Headset status over Wi-Fi (optional)" once while
+   the cable is in; after that it works over Wi-Fi until the headset restarts.
