+// [arroom] AR room collision: the arena's collision world is replaced by the player's real room.
+//
+// The room is Mario Tabletop's detailed scan (aether-room-play.bin, 'ARP1': anchor-local OpenXR triangles,
+// counter-clockwise seen from the open side). It is written once into the guest's extra RAM (above the 32 MB the
+// game sees) in BT3's own collision-mesh format, and every frame each arena cell is pointed at it with its object
+// list emptied. The game's collision code then runs unchanged against the room: landing on the desk, crashing into
+// the monitor, bouncing off the PC -- with the game's own reactions.
+//
+// BT3 collision, read out of SLUS_216.78 (2026-10-20):
+//   stage header  *(gp-0x5690): +0x38 cell count (10 x 10), +0x3C cells (64 bytes each)
+//   cell          +0x04 ground mesh, +0x14 object count, +0x18 object list; +0x20/+0x28 centre x/z, +0x30/+0x38 half size
+//   pool          *(gp-0x56E0) = the stage file; mesh offsets are in WORDS from it
+//   mesh header   +0x00 node count, +0x04 triangle count, +0x08 0, +0x0C node / +0x10 triangle / +0x14 vertex offset,
+//                 +0x18 AABB min xyz, +0x24 AABB max xyz  (0x30 bytes)
+//   vertex        x, y, z, 1 (16 bytes)
+//   triangle      flags (0x10000002 = terrain), i0, i1, i2, n.xyz, d  (32 bytes); n = normalize(cross(v1-v0, v2-v0))
+//                 points to the open side, d = n . v0
+//   BVH node      AABB min xyz, max xyz, +0x18 left child | triangle, +0x1C right child | -1 = leaf  (32 bytes), root 0
+//   walkers       0x231768 / 0x231670 (tree), leaf test FUN_001b1900 -> 0x236228 (sphere vs triangle)
+// Game space: up = -y, a fighter is ~12 units tall; the arena centre is the origin.
+//
+// Environment:
+//   PS2X_AR_SCAN=<path>          the ARP1 file (off when unset)
+//   PS2X_AR_UNITS_PER_M=<f>      game units per metre (default 59: a 20 cm fighter)
+//   PS2X_AR_ORIGIN=x,y,z         room point (metres, y-up room space) that becomes the arena centre (default: the desk)
+//   PS2X_AR_YAW=<deg>            arena rotation about up
+//   PS2X_AR_ANCHOR_UP=z|y        which anchor-local axis is up (default z; the headset build passes the anchor pose)
